{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"verdict\": \"both_partly\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"DOPAOFF, 12 patients with PD had FOG observed (FOG‐OBS, 263 episodes), occurring at a mean of 8 steps after GI, and 26 had no FOG observed (NOBS; FOG‐NOBS).\",\n    \"In the 12 FOG‐OBS patients with PD, we recorded 99 trials where a FOG event occurred in the DOPAOFF condition (FOG‐OBS+ trials), with a median onset of 8 steps (interquartile range [IQR] = 6–11.5) after GI, and a total of 263 FOG episodes (Fig 1E–G).\",\n    \"These FOG‐OBS patients also completed 212 walking trials without FOG (FOG‐OBS− trials; see Fig 1E).\",\n    \"We first examined the relationship between LFP spectral power and GI RPC scores in trials without FOG, in the DOPAOFF condition, in both patients with PD groups (Supplementary Fig S3).\",\n    \"To explore STN dysfunction linked to FOG, we compared trials with freezing (FOG‐OBS+ trials) to those without (FOG‐OBS− trials) in FOG‐OBS patients with PD (DOPAOFF condition; Fig 6).\",\n    \"These changes were evident as early as the GI phase, prior to the observable FOG onset.\",\n    \"Our results support the existence of a predisposed state for FOG at gait initiation, which may be partially mitigated through compensatory mechanisms involving widespread low‐beta modulations within the STN; and an actual occurrence of FOG, marked by an early modulation in high‐beta activity in the posterior STN.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"两方各有部分依据。报告正确的部分是：论文的主要神经电生理分析确实集中在步态启动（GI）阶段，且相当一部分分析使用没有发生FOG的试次，研究重点包括FOG易感状态与STN活动的关系。论文明确指出首先分析了没有FOG的试次中的LFP与GI参数关系。此外，冻结通常发生在步态启动后数步，因此GI阶段记录的神经信号不能称为冻结实际发生期间（During-FOG）的直接神经活动记录。但报告的表述如果意味着研究只分析了没有冻结的试次，或者其证据仅属于一般FOG易感性，则不准确。原文明确报告12名患者发生了263次冻结事件，分布于99个FOG阳性步行试次；同时还专门设置了Predictive Patterns of FOG Occurrence分析，比较同一批FOG观察阳性患者中最终发生冻结与没有发生冻结的试次，并分析两类试次在步态启动阶段的STN-LFP差异。讨论进一步明确指出，这些神经活动变化在可观察到冻结之前的GI阶段已经出现。因此，指控者正确指出研究包含冻结前、事件相关的神经活动证据，而不只是FOG易感性证据；但不能据此将其归类为冻结期间的直接神经活动证据。综合而言，报告对研究主要分析窗口及非During-FOG性质的判断基本正确，但对冻结阳性试次及其事件相关分析的证据性质有所简化；指控者对这部分遗漏的批评成立，但若将其理解为冻结期间的直接神经记录则不成立。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "250f64b6-54db-43d9-b184-7c014389530c", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T104554715335Z", "elapsed_seconds": 57.625, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T10:46:52.353018+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "29cab8fbac4a1cfa8e217af1046948bbb7664c67456c2b0b1bacf37b8ee5ce47", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "Nozomi Kasaki / gpt4", "account_sha256": "bbd4fd636d4b6714d2b42b89e341bdb5bbe7c34f7d141aec76b444be8343fe54", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T104554715335Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "2ec231e8eeb9c6027edf8661b4ef711ba81f174b66db10db5baabe22fd1a1242"}}}
